Subject: composer: restart SurfaceFlinger when the composer comes back

SurfaceFlinger resolves the composer service exactly once, at its own
start, and carries no death recipient for it: a composer that dies
leaves SF holding a proxy to a node that no longer exists, every call
answering an error it reads as "no resources", the screen frozen until
someone restarts SF by hand. That is unchanged through Android 22 --
the fix has always lived in init, not in code, and hwc3-pixel.rc
carries exactly this line. The stock direction (SF stopped -> restart
HWC) stays; the two do not loop, because a restart passes through
"restarting", never "stopped".

--- a/graphics/composer/2.1/default/android.hardware.graphics.composer@2.1-service.rc
+++ b/graphics/composer/2.1/default/android.hardware.graphics.composer@2.1-service.rc
@@ -4,6 +4,12 @@
     group graphics drmrpc
     capabilities SYS_NICE
     writepid /dev/cpuset/system-background/tasks
+    # A dead composer leaves SurfaceFlinger holding a proxy to a node that
+    # no longer exists: it never re-resolves the service, every call returns
+    # an error that reads as "no resources", and the screen stays frozen
+    # until someone restarts it by hand. Restarting it here closes the loop
+    # the moment the composer comes back, the way hwc3-pixel.rc does.
+    onrestart restart surfaceflinger
 
 # Restart HWC when SurfaceFlinger stops. This turns off the display and prpares
 # a new HWC instance for when SurfaceFlinger gets started again
